          "from": "Proto-Georgian-Zan *s₁owel- 'wet' (Old Georgian სუელი sueli)",
          "to": "Laz შუვი šuvi, Mingrelian შუ šu",
          "note": "Georgian has s in the same roots. Wiktionary's subscript-1 series (*s₁, *z₁, *c₁, *ʒ₁) is the Gamkrelidze-Machavariani 'hissing-hushing' series, given in the Wikipedia Proto-Kartvelian consonant table (after Gamkrelidze 1966 and Fähnrich 2002) as retroflex [ʂ ʐ ʈ͡ʂ ɖ͡ʐ]."
